Composer like ChatGPT, Claude and Qwen Chat (#138, research on #135): one + menu, a speed selector, PDF, documents.
- «سريع / متأنٍّ / عميق» (SpeedSelector.tsx) in place of the model button and the «تفكير» switch: one choice named by
  its outcome, each option one of the three lineup specs («بصير لايت / بلس / برو» under it, with its description).
  The chat switches in place. Any other spec (an agent, an upstream configuration) keeps the upstream model button.
  ThinkingToggle.tsx is gone.
- «+» (ToolsDropdown.tsx) holds the composer's tools: «إرفاق ملف» (opens the upstream upload control, kept in the DOM
  but out of view), then on/off items with a check mark: «مستندات» (artifacts), «الإنترنت», skills, memory. The pin
  buttons, the artifacts sub-menu and its shadcn/ui and custom prompt modes are gone; a chat left in one of those
  modes returns to the default mode. A tool that is on shows as a chip, and tapping the chip turns it off.
- «الإنترنت» (composerModes.ts, InternetBadge.tsx): every speed has a hidden twin spec on an endpoint without the
  provider's search (librechat.yaml, `showInMenu: false`). The server keeps hidden specs out of the browser's config
  and resolves them by name, so the client builds the twin from the visible spec and switches to it in place.
- «PDF / طباعة» under «تنزيل» (DownloadReply.tsx, utils/efaiwPrint.ts): the reply in a print view in a new tab, right
  to left when written in Arabic, A4, then the browser's print dialog (save as PDF on a phone too). Built with the
  same Markdown parser as the Word file; the page has no script of its own.
- A document the reply is writing opens in the side panel by itself (Artifact.tsx), only while that reply streams.

